# qt-qalculate (Qalculate! 5.12.0, the Qt GUI, as a wk node). Upstream is
# FETCHED by build.sh, never vendored -- and here that is SIX upstreams:
# qalculate-qt, libqalculate, gmp, mpfr, libxml2 and the qtsvg Qt module.
# ./sysroot is this port's own install prefix, holding both the four C/C++
# dependencies and Qt6::Svg, layered on plugins/qt/sysroot; nothing here ever
# writes into plugins/qt. Only build.sh, mise.toml, cmake/, patches/,
# harness/, doc/, example.wk, Dockerfile and PORTING.md are tracked.
plugins/qt-qalculate/tarballs/
plugins/qt-qalculate/src/
plugins/qt-qalculate/build/
plugins/qt-qalculate/sysroot/
plugins/qt-qalculate/gen/
plugins/qt-qalculate/logs/
plugins/qt-qalculate/*.wasm
plugins/qt-qalculate/harness/target/
# A copy of somebody else's font, staged by build.sh from whatever the machine
# has. Qt 6 ships no fonts and a wk node has no host font dir, so the app
# compiles one in as a Qt resource -- but the file itself is not ours to commit.
plugins/qt-qalculate/fonts/

# qt-kcalc (KCalc + the fourteen KDE Frameworks it needs, as a wk node).
# Upstream is FETCHED by build.sh, never vendored: the KF6 repos are shallow
# clones pinned to v6.24.0 under src/, and qtsvg/zlib/gmp/mpfr/mpc/kcalc come
# from tarballs/. ./sysroot is this port's own install prefix layered on
# plugins/qt/sysroot (extra Qt modules + every KF6 library); ./host holds the
# native extra-cmake-modules install, which is pure CMake and must not be
# confused with plugins/qt/host. Only build.sh, patches/, mise.toml and
# PORTING.md are tracked.
plugins/qt-kcalc/tarballs/
plugins/qt-kcalc/src/
plugins/qt-kcalc/build/
plugins/qt-kcalc/sysroot/
plugins/qt-kcalc/host/
# A NATIVE kconfig_compiler, kept in its own prefix and deliberately OFF the
# app's CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH -- see the kconfighost stage in build.sh.
plugins/qt-kcalc/host-tooling/
plugins/qt-kcalc/gen/
plugins/qt-kcalc/logs/
plugins/qt-kcalc/*.wasm
plugins/qt-kcalc/harness/target/
# A copy of somebody else's font, staged by build.sh from whatever the machine
# has. Qt 6 ships no fonts and a wk node has no host font dir, so the app
# compiles one in as a Qt resource -- but the file itself is not ours to commit.
plugins/qt-kcalc/fonts/

# qt-drumstickvpiano2111 (drumstick-vpiano 2.11.1 as a wk node: a real Qt 6
